        "original_id": "005fb76f-c5c9-54dc-9c6d-590af9e8e480",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Pound Ridge massacre, Kieft's War\n- People: Captain John Underhill\n- Groups: Dutch and English soldiers, Lenape, settlers of New Netherland\n- Places: Pound Ridge, New Netherland, New York metropolitan area\n\nFacts:\n- Kieft's War, also known as the Wappinger War, was a conflict from 1643 to 1645 between settlers of the colony of New Netherland and the native Lenape population in the area that later became the New York metropolitan area of the United States.\n- During the Pound Ridge massacre, a mixed force of 130 Dutch and English soldiers led by Captain John Underhill launched a night attack on a village and destroyed it by fire.\n- The Pound Ridge massacre caused more casualties than any other single incident in Kieft's War.",
